  "title": "Qt: Treat IO Graphs with lines and data points as line graphs",
  "description": "Commit edf48633bbf5d8057e1929ef997d78eaad01351f added some\nstyles that have both lines and symbols for each data point\n(a scatter style). Treat those as line graphs for the purposes\nof displaying zero values instead of as scatter plots, so change\nthe test for if a graph is a scatter plot from \"if the scatter\nstyle is not none\" to \"if the line style is not none\" to reflect that.\n\n(Cf.\nhttps://www.wireshark.org/docs/wsug_html_chunked/ChStatIOGraphs.html#ChStatIOGraphsMissingValues\n\"For scatter plots it is assumed that zero values indicate missing\ndata, and those values are omitted. Zero values are shown in line\ngraphs, and bar charts.\" )",
